Z||000000||1FST2M6||11-09-2001||12:17 PM||||well ya don't have to be really smart.. but how can i get this stupid camera to take better night time low light pics? i don't know how to adjust the pseudo-shutter speed on a digital camera... it's a mavica fd-85 does vidoe and such...<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstdark.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstlight.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>0-60 in 4.91<P> <A HREF="http://www.1fst2m6.com" TARGET=_blank>www.1fst2m6.com</A>  - underconstruction - but check it out anywho...||||reg||1
Z||000001||MinnGreenGT||11-09-2001||01:04 PM||||Well, in this case- smart has nothing to do with it.  Most digital cameras are not designed to handle night time conditions.  They're shutter systems just don't do well with it.  (I tried too).  Technically it really depends on your camera.  <B>If</B> you can specific a long/slow shutter speed with a large aperture (smaller number...larger opening). Then you will get better results.  The difficulty with this is blurring.  You'll need to shoot from a tripod.  Anyway- the option is to just "photoshop the heck out 'em"<P>This is just a few quick tweaks...nothing spectacular.  Good luck!<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstdark_01.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phil||11-09-2001||01:24 PM||||I only have 35m/m cameras but don't digital cameras have a flash attachment?||||reg||1
Z||000003||1FST2M6||11-09-2001||01:30 PM||||the original pic was MUCH darker than what i posted... thats why it's grainy... photshop is king.. but i want the real thing. LOL.. that rhymed.. anyway..  i shut the flash off... My my cannon takes ok night pics on a tripod but i don't wanna have to wait for them to be develpoed to post em or e-mail them. i'm looking for instant gratification. oh well guess i'll just have to suck it up and deal with darker digital pics.  thanks though guys... ||||reg||1
Z||000004||CoolBlue87GT||11-09-2001||01:31 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 1FST2M6:<BR><B>how can i get this stupid camera to take better night time low light pics?<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I've got the Sony Mavica CD300. You could try using the SCN setting, then select twilight mode.<P>Might want to use a tripod, as the shutter stays open longer. (I've used it without, and had good results)<P>Good luck.<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000005||MinnGreenGT||11-09-2001||01:40 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 1FST2M6:<BR><B>My my cannon takes ok night pics on a tripod...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Cannon EOS systems rule!  That's it, you could get a Canon EOS D30  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> It'll take nice night photos, it operates just like a normal Canon, but with digital.  Ok, Yeah, the D30 is around $2k without any lens... oh well- Good luck.||||reg||1
